# Example environment file - SAFE TO COMMIT, because it contains no values.
#
# Copy the lines you need into `.env.development` (read by run_dev.bat) or `.env` on the
# server, and fill them in there. Every real env file is gitignored: a secret is compromised
# the moment it is committed, not when someone notices.

# --- required ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/dbname
# SESSION_SECRET=<a long random string; `python -c "import secrets;print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"`>

# --- Google Sign-In (see GoogleAuthSetup.md) --------------------------------------------
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- optional: language-model fallback for the Match tab --------------------------------
# Off unless LLM_EXTRACT_ENABLED and a key are BOTH set. While off, the Match tab behaves
# exactly as it always has. See app/llm_extract.py for what it does and does not do.
#
# It is asked only about requirement blocks the regexes did poorly on (3 of 52 fixtures on
# the sample SampleClient PDF), and may only ADD fields they missed, never overwrite one. Any
# failure - timeout, quota, bad response - returns the regex result unchanged.
#
# LLM_EXTRACT_ENABLED=1
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# LLM_EXTRACT_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile
# LLM_EXTRACT_MIN_FIELDS=7
